exercises.prompt:
Prove the mental model from the identity lesson: calling a component function twice yields two DISTINCT element objects with structurally EQUAL content, and new props yield a new element rather than mutating the old one.

Example:
```js
function Greeting({ name }) {
  return { type: 'h1', props: { children: 'Hello, ' + name } };
}

const first = Greeting({ name: 'Ada' });
const second = Greeting({ name: 'Ada' });
const third = Greeting({ name: 'Grace' });

console.log('distinct objects:', first !== second);
assert.deepStrictEqual(first, second);
console.log('structurally equal:', true);
console.log('new props, new element:', third !== first);
console.log('old element unmutated:', first.props.children === 'Hello, Ada');
console.log('fresh content:', third.props.children);
```
Expected output:
```
distinct objects: true
structurally equal: true
new props, new element: true
old element unmutated: true
fresh content: Hello, Grace
```

